{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ONE PHOTO SLOT — real image, or the decided fallback (GAPS §8 Q8, owner, 4 Oct 2026)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Every page asks "what goes here when there is no photo?" and every page used to answer
  it differently (initials on one, a continent outline on another, a gradient on a third).
  This partial is the one answer:

    · a real image ............ shown, `object-fit: cover`, filling the slot the caller sized
    · PEOPLE without one ...... a monogram: up to two initials in Playfair 700, ink on the
                                neutral `tint` ground, inside a hairline ring. Never an
                                invented face, never a stock photo, never a broken-image box.
    · THINGS without one ...... a generated cover (events, campaigns, awards, products): the
                                thing's own accent through EventFlierTheme — PhotoCover::style()
                                hands the four contrast-checked colours in as custom properties
                                (`tone`), so nothing here is a hex — with the title set in it.
                                Without a tone the cover is drawn in the house ink family.
                                Drawn in CSS, so it is never a request that can fail.

  Args (with … only):
    kind     'person' | 'thing'                       required
    src      image URL, or empty                     the caller validates it (EventTicketDesign::image)
    name     the person's name, or the thing's title  required — the initials and the cover title
    ini      the person's initials, where the caller already holds them (HomeFront::initials,
             which skips a leading mark of punctuation); otherwise worked out from `name`
    alt      text alternative for a real image        default '' (decorative)
    tone     PhotoCover::style() string              things only; optional
    title    false to set no title in a cover        default true (off for small slots)
    eager    true for the largest above-the-fold paint (no lazy loading)
    class    extra classes on the slot

  The slot fills its container: the CALLER decides the size and the aspect ratio, because a
  4:3 hero, a 52px row thumb and a 44px avatar are different decisions made by their pages.
  A slot that names a person or a thing in words beside it should pass no `alt` — the
  name is said once, not twice.
#}
{%- set _person = (kind|default('thing')) == 'person' -%}
{%- set _src = src|default('') -%}
{%- set _ini = ini|default(name|default('')|split(' ')|filter(w => w|trim != '')|map(w => w|first)|join|upper|slice(0, 2)) -%}
{%- if _src -%}
<span class="ag-photo{{ _person ? ' ag-photo--person' }}{{ class is defined ? ' ' ~ class }}">
  <img class="ag-photo__img" src="{{ _src }}" alt="{{ alt|default('') }}"{% if eager|default(false) %} fetchpriority="high"{% else %} loading="lazy"{% endif %} decoding="async">
</span>
{%- elseif _person -%}
<span class="ag-photo ag-photo--person ag-photo--mono{{ class is defined ? ' ' ~ class }}"{% if alt|default('') %} role="img" aria-label="{{ alt }}"{% else %} aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>
  <span class="ag-photo__ini">{{ _ini }}</span>
</span>
{%- else -%}
<span class="ag-photo ag-photo--cover{{ class is defined ? ' ' ~ class }}"{% if tone|default('') %} style="{{ tone }}"{% endif %}{% if alt|default('') %} role="img" aria-label="{{ alt }}"{% else %} aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>
  {%- if title|default(true) %}<span class="ag-photo__rule"></span><span class="ag-photo__title">{{ name }}</span>{% endif -%}
</span>
{%- endif -%}
